{
  "suite": "membership",
  "level": 4,
  "about": "Changing what a collection holds and where it holds it. A collection owns placement and owns everything on it that is not an object, so all three of these are writes against the collection rather than patches on anything in it.",
  "requires": {
    "features": [
      "placement"
    ]
  },
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "membership/context-merges",
      "level": 4,
      "op": "place",
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "id": "c_board",
          "kind": "canvas",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": false
          }
        },
        "member": {
          "object": "o_1",
          "context": {
            "x": 340,
            "y": 120,
            "w": 280,
            "h": 190,
            "hermes:color": "#fdf3d8"
          }
        },
        "patch": {
          "context": {
            "x": 400
          }
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": true,
        "member": {
          "object": "o_1",
          "context": {
            "x": 400,
            "y": 120,
            "w": 280,
            "h": 190,
            "hermes:color": "#fdf3d8"
          }
        }
      },
      "why": "The round-trip rule at write time, in the place it is most often skipped. A tool that drags a card sends the two numbers it moved; the size and the color were put there by something else and it has never heard of them. A write that replaced the bag would delete them, and the caller would be told it succeeded."
    },
    {
      "id": "membership/unset-is-the-only-way-to-remove",
      "level": 4,
      "op": "place",
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "id": "c_board",
          "kind": "canvas",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": false
          }
        },
        "member": {
          "object": "o_1",
          "context": {
            "x": 340,
            "y": 120,
            "hermes:collapsed": true
          }
        },
        "patch": {
          "unset": [
            "hermes:collapsed"
          ]
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": true,
        "member": {
          "object": "o_1",
          "context": {
            "x": 340,
            "y": 120
          }
        }
      },
      "why": "Same two moves as a patch on an object and for the same reason: a key named by neither `context` nor `unset` is untouched, so removing one has to be said out loud. Sending it as null would collide with every model where null is a value somebody chose."
    },
    {
      "id": "membership/furniture-can-be-emptied-completely",
      "level": 4,
      "op": "place",
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "id": "c_board",
          "kind": "canvas",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": false
          }
        },
        "member": {
          "object": "o_1",
          "context": {
            "x": 340,
            "y": 120
          }
        },
        "patch": {
          "unset": [
            "x",
            "y"
          ]
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": true,
        "member": {
          "object": "o_1",
          "context": null
        }
      },
      "why": "A member that has had all its furniture removed carries no bag, not an empty one. An empty object is a fact about nothing that the round-trip rule would then be obliged to preserve forever."
    },
    {
      "id": "membership/coordinates-refused-on-semantic-placement",
      "level": 4,
      "op": "place",
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "id": "c_priorities",
          "kind": "matrix",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": true,
            "regions": [
              "urgent-important",
              "calm-later"
            ]
          }
        },
        "member": {
          "object": "o_1",
          "region": "urgent-important"
        },
        "patch": {
          "context": {
            "x": 340,
            "y": 120
          }
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": false,
        "reports": [
          "placement.coordinates-not-semantic"
        ]
      },
      "why": "The same rule the validator enforces on a document, enforced on a write. A coordinate means nothing outside the grid that produced it, so a judgment recorded as one is a judgment nothing else can read. Refused rather than stored, because stored-and-unreadable looks exactly like success."
    },
    {
      "id": "membership/region-must-be-one-the-collection-declared",
      "level": 4,
      "op": "place",
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "id": "c_priorities",
          "kind": "matrix",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": true,
            "regions": [
              "urgent-important",
              "calm-later"
            ]
          }
        },
        "member": {
          "object": "o_1",
          "region": "urgent-important"
        },
        "patch": {
          "region": "someday"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": false,
        "reports": [
          "placement.region-not-declared"
        ]
      },
      "why": "A region nothing renders is a card that has vanished from the board with nobody told. The write knows which regions exist \u2014 they are on the collection it is written against \u2014 so it is the last place this can be caught."
    },
    {
      "id": "membership/region-null-is-still-a-member",
      "level": 4,
      "op": "place",
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "id": "c_priorities",
          "kind": "matrix",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": true,
            "regions": [
              "urgent-important",
              "calm-later"
            ]
          }
        },
        "member": {
          "object": "o_1",
          "region": "urgent-important"
        },
        "patch": {
          "region": null
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": true,
        "member": {
          "object": "o_1"
        }
      },
      "why": "Added but not placed is a real state \u2014 a card in the drawer beside the board \u2014 and it is not the same as not being on the board at all. Null is admissible here, unlike in `context`, because a region is one slot rather than a bag: there is no value it could be confused with."
    },
    {
      "id": "membership/a-stale-move-is-refused",
      "level": 4,
      "op": "place",
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "id": "c_board",
          "kind": "canvas",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": false
          }
        },
        "member": {
          "object": "o_1",
          "version": 7,
          "context": {
            "x": 340
          }
        },
        "patch": {
          "context": {
            "x": 400
          },
          "version": 6
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": false,
        "conflict": true
      },
      "why": "Merging a stale move is how one person's drag silently reverts another's, with the writer told it landed. A producer that versions memberships must refuse; one that does not version them accepts, which is a weaker promise honestly made rather than a stronger one pretended to."
    },
    {
      "id": "membership/a-move-answers-with-the-next-version",
      "level": 4,
      "op": "place",
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "id": "c_board",
          "kind": "canvas",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": false
          }
        },
        "member": {
          "object": "o_1",
          "version": 7,
          "context": {
            "x": 340
          }
        },
        "patch": {
          "context": {
            "x": 400
          },
          "version": 7
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": true,
        "member": {
          "object": "o_1",
          "version": 8,
          "context": {
            "x": 400
          }
        }
      },
      "why": "A client that drags a card twice must not have to re-read the board between drags. If the answer does not carry the version the write produced, the second drag sends the first one's number and is refused as stale \u2014 so a producer that versions memberships and answers without one has built a board that can be moved once. This is the same rule as a write answering with its object, applied to the thing that is actually contended."
    },
    {
      "id": "membership/an-unversioned-membership-accepts-anything",
      "level": 4,
      "op": "place",
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "id": "c_board",
          "kind": "canvas",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": false
          }
        },
        "member": {
          "object": "o_1",
          "context": {
            "x": 340
          }
        },
        "patch": {
          "context": {
            "x": 400
          },
          "version": 3
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": true,
        "member": {
          "object": "o_1",
          "context": {
            "x": 400
          }
        }
      },
      "why": "A producer that does not version memberships says so by never issuing one, and must then accept whatever a hopeful client sends rather than refusing on a number it does not keep. The answer carries no version either \u2014 inventing one here would tell the client it is protected when nothing is comparing. A weaker promise honestly made."
    },
    {
      "id": "membership/put-makes-a-membership",
      "level": 4,
      "op": "member",
      "args": {
        "object": "o_2",
        "op": "put"
      },
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "id": "c_board",
          "kind": "canvas",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": false
          },
          "members": [
            {
              "object": "o_1",
              "context": {
                "x": 0,
                "y": 0
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "patch": {
          "context": {
            "x": 340,
            "y": 120
          }
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": true,
        "created": true,
        "member": {
          "object": "o_2",
          "context": {
            "x": 340,
            "y": 120
          }
        }
      },
      "why": "Adding something to a board is the write that was missing: everything else assumed the membership already existed. It arrives with its placement, because a card that appears and then jumps to where it belongs is two states a viewer sees and only one of them is real."
    },
    {
      "id": "membership/put-again-changes-nothing",
      "level": 4,
      "op": "member",
      "args": {
        "object": "o_1",
        "op": "put"
      },
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "id": "c_board",
          "kind": "canvas",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": false
          },
          "members": [
            {
              "object": "o_1",
              "context": {
                "x": 340,
                "y": 120
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "patch": {
          "context": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0
          }
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": true,
        "created": false,
        "member": {
          "object": "o_1",
          "context": {
            "x": 340,
            "y": 120
          }
        }
      },
      "why": "The same division `PUT` and `PATCH` draw on an object, for the same reason. This is a caller asking again because it never heard the first answer, not a caller asking for the card to be moved back to the origin \u2014 and a verb that did both could not be retried after a timeout."
    },
    {
      "id": "membership/put-refuses-a-region-nobody-declared",
      "level": 4,
      "op": "member",
      "args": {
        "object": "o_2",
        "op": "put"
      },
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "id": "c_priorities",
          "kind": "matrix",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": true,
            "regions": [
              "urgent-important",
              "calm-later"
            ]
          },
          "members": []
        },
        "patch": {
          "region": "someday"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": false,
        "created": false,
        "reports": [
          "placement.region-not-declared"
        ]
      },
      "why": "Arriving somewhere that does not exist is the same failure as moving somewhere that does not exist, so it is the same rule and must not be a second copy of it. A board that accepts the create and drops the region has silently added an invisible card."
    },
    {
      "id": "membership/delete-unmakes-the-membership-not-the-object",
      "level": 4,
      "op": "member",
      "args": {
        "object": "o_1",
        "op": "delete"
      },
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "id": "c_board",
          "kind": "canvas",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": false
          },
          "members": [
            {
              "object": "o_1"
            },
            {
              "object": "o_2"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": true,
        "removed": true
      },
      "why": "The one write where the difference between taking something off a list and destroying it has to be carried by the verb. The object goes on existing wherever else it lives; this write is handed the collection and nothing else, which is the shape that makes deleting the object impossible rather than merely discouraged."
    },
    {
      "id": "membership/delete-again-is-a-success",
      "level": 4,
      "op": "member",
      "args": {
        "object": "o_9",
        "op": "delete"
      },
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "id": "c_board",
          "kind": "canvas",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": false
          },
          "members": [
            {
              "object": "o_1"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": true,
        "removed": false
      },
      "why": "Not a member, and the caller wanted it not to be: that is the state it asked for. Answering not-found makes every offline client special-case its own retries, which is where the duplicate-and-vanish bugs come from."
    },
    {
      "id": "membership/a-collections-own-keys-must-be-prefixed",
      "level": 4,
      "op": "collectionPatch",
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "id": "c_board",
          "kind": "canvas",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": false
          },
          "properties": {
            "hermes:canvas_notes": []
          }
        },
        "patch": {
          "set": {
            "canvas_notes": [
              {
                "id": "n:1",
                "text": "hello"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": false,
        "reports": [
          "collection.unprefixed-write"
        ]
      },
      "why": "Unprefixed names on a collection belong to the format, and this is the write that would otherwise let a producer take one without anybody noticing. It is the same failure the prefix rule was written for, arriving through the one door that rule had not been applied to."
    },
    {
      "id": "membership/the-formats-namespace-is-not-writable-here",
      "level": 4,
      "op": "collectionPatch",
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "id": "c_board",
          "kind": "canvas",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": false
          },
          "properties": {
            "hermes:sort_mode": "created"
          }
        },
        "patch": {
          "set": {
            "sort_mode": "alpha"
          }
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": false,
        "reports": [
          "collection.unprefixed-write"
        ]
      },
      "why": "Not an abstraction. Hermes was spending twenty-nine unprefixed names on collections, `sort_mode` and `table_sort` among them \u2014 this document's own open limit, no sort or grouping on a collection, being solved privately under the name v0.1 would want. This write is the door that rule had not been applied to. The collection's structural keys need no rule of their own: `kind`, `placement` and `members` are not in `properties` and are unreachable from here, which is stronger than refusing them."
    },
    {
      "id": "membership/a-collection-write-leaves-the-rest-alone",
      "level": 4,
      "op": "collectionPatch",
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "id": "c_board",
          "kind": "canvas",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": false
          },
          "properties": {
            "hermes:canvas_notes": [],
            "hermes:table_sort": "created",
            "obsidian:folder": "Boards"
          }
        },
        "patch": {
          "set": {
            "hermes:canvas_notes": [
              {
                "id": "n:1",
                "text": "hello"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": true,
        "collection": {
          "properties": {
            "hermes:canvas_notes": [
              {
                "id": "n:1",
                "text": "hello"
              }
            ],
            "hermes:table_sort": "created",
            "obsidian:folder": "Boards"
          }
        },
        "keys": [
          "hermes:canvas_notes",
          "hermes:table_sort",
          "obsidian:folder"
        ]
      },
      "why": "The reason this write exists at all is a canvas's sticky notes, which are not objects and can be written no other way. It must not become the reason another producer's keys disappear \u2014 including the keys of a producer this one has never heard of."
    },
    {
      "id": "membership/unset-removes-one-key-and-only-one",
      "level": 4,
      "op": "collectionPatch",
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "id": "c_board",
          "kind": "canvas",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": false
          },
          "properties": {
            "hermes:canvas_notes": [
              {
                "id": "n:1",
                "text": "hello"
              }
            ],
            "hermes:canvas_edges": []
          }
        },
        "patch": {
          "unset": [
            "hermes:canvas_notes"
          ]
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": true,
        "collection": {
          "properties": {
            "hermes:canvas_edges": []
          }
        },
        "keys": [
          "hermes:canvas_edges"
        ]
      },
      "why": "Set and unset, with the meaning they have everywhere else in this document. Stated as its own case because a bag-shaped write is exactly where an implementation is tempted to treat the payload as the whole object."
    },
    {
      "id": "membership/a-collection-can-be-brought-into-being",
      "level": 4,
      "op": "collectionCreate",
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "id": "c_scratch",
          "name": "Scratch canvas",
          "kind": "canvas",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": false
          }
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": true,
        "created": true,
        "collection": {
          "id": "c_scratch",
          "name": "Scratch canvas",
          "kind": "canvas",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": false
          }
        }
      },
      "why": "A client that keeps a document of its own has to be able to make the container the first time it runs. Without this the format could arrange a collection, write its keys, add and remove its members, and not make one \u2014 so every client that needed a place to put things reached past the format for the one call that starts everything, which is the call most worth having in it."
    },
    {
      "id": "membership/the-client-chooses-the-collection-id",
      "level": 4,
      "op": "collectionCreate",
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "name": "Scratch canvas",
          "kind": "canvas"
        },
        "args": {
          "at": "c_scratch"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": true,
        "created": true,
        "collection": {
          "id": "c_scratch",
          "kind": "canvas"
        }
      },
      "why": "An id decided before the request is what makes a repeat recognizable as a repeat. A client that could not name the collection it was making would have to ask what it got, and a lost answer would leave it unable to tell a retry from a second board."
    },
    {
      "id": "membership/repeating-a-collection-create-is-not-a-second-board",
      "level": 4,
      "op": "collectionCreate",
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "id": "c_scratch",
          "name": "Scratch canvas",
          "kind": "canvas",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": false
          }
        },
        "existing": {
          "id": "c_scratch",
          "name": "Scratch canvas",
          "kind": "canvas",
          "placement": {
            "semantic": false
          },
          "properties": {
            "talaria:regions": [
              {
                "title": "Ideas"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": true,
        "created": false,
        "collection": {
          "properties": {
            "talaria:regions": [
              {
                "title": "Ideas"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "why": "The check-and-create a client runs at startup is this exact call, every time it starts. It succeeded once; this is the caller asking again because it never heard so, and answering with a fresh empty board would throw away everything on it."
    },
    {
      "id": "membership/a-collection-create-does-not-replace",
      "level": 4,
      "op": "collectionCreate",
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "id": "c_scratch",
          "kind": "canvas",
          "name": "Renamed"
        },
        "existing": {
          "id": "c_scratch",
          "kind": "canvas",
          "name": "Scratch canvas",
          "properties": {
            "hermes:sort_mode": "manual"
          }
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": true,
        "created": false,
        "collection": {
          "name": "Scratch canvas",
          "properties": {
            "hermes:sort_mode": "manual"
          }
        }
      },
      "why": "The round-trip rule at write time, by the verb least likely to be suspected of it. A create that replaced would discard every key the caller had never heard of \u2014 and a caller repeating a create has by definition not read what is there. Renaming is what a patch is for."
    },
    {
      "id": "membership/two-collection-ids-is-a-refusal",
      "level": 4,
      "op": "collectionCreate",
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "id": "c_one",
          "kind": "canvas"
        },
        "args": {
          "at": "c_two"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": false,
        "created": false,
        "reports": [
          "create.id-mismatch"
        ]
      },
      "why": "Two ids in one request is a caller's bug, and either reading is obviously right. Choosing between them silently is how a board is made somewhere nobody will look for it."
    },
    {
      "id": "membership/a-created-collection-cannot-take-an-unprefixed-key",
      "level": 4,
      "op": "collectionCreate",
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "id": "c_scratch",
          "kind": "canvas",
          "properties": {
            "sort_mode": "manual"
          }
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": false,
        "created": false,
        "reports": [
          "collection.unprefixed-write"
        ]
      },
      "why": "The prefix rule reaches this door too. A patch refuses an unprefixed key because unprefixed names belong to the format; a create that did not would be the way around it \u2014 make the collection with the key already on it and no write ever has to be refused."
    },
    {
      "id": "membership/members-do-not-arrive-with-a-collection",
      "level": 4,
      "op": "collectionCreate",
      "given": {
        "collection": {
          "id": "c_scratch",
          "kind": "canvas",
          "members": [
            {
              "object": "o_1"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": false,
        "created": false,
        "reports": [
          "collection.members-are-a-separate-write"
        ]
      },
      "why": "Joining a collection can tag a card, move it, or change its status \u2014 a region declares what it does to what lands in it \u2014 and a bag of ids carried along with a create cannot say whether any of that ran. Refused rather than dropped: a caller whose members vanished quietly would believe the board was full."
    }
  ]
}
